{"seq":2,"slug":"logic","title":"逻辑学","stage":"DONE","chapterCount":4,"docCount":12,"url":"/education/university/philosophy/logic","introMarkdown":"# 逻辑学 简介\n\n逻辑学研究推理的有效结构与论证的评估标准，它为数学证明、计算机科学、法律论辩乃至日常决策提供共同的推理框架。掌握逻辑，意味着能够将模糊的直觉转化为清晰的推理链条，并在面对复杂信息时识别隐藏的谬误。\n\n本知识体系从符号化的精确推演到日常语境中的论证分析，再到逻辑在前沿领域的具体应用，构建一条从基础到实践的完整学习路径。\n\n第一章**形式逻辑**从命题逻辑的真值表与推理规则入手，进而引入谓词逻辑的量词与变元，最后拓展到模态逻辑对\"可能\"与\"必然\"的刻画，为严格的符号推理奠定基础。\n\n第二章**非形式逻辑**将视角从公式转向自然语言中的论证，讨论论证结构的识别与评价、常见逻辑谬误的类型，以及批判性思维的核心策略，帮助自学者在写作和辩论中提升论证质量。\n\n第三章**数理逻辑**探讨集合论公理体系、模型论中语言与结构的对应关系，以及可计算性理论所揭示的推理能力的根本界限，这些内容构成现代数学和理论计算机科学的基石。\n\n第四章**应用逻辑**展示逻辑如何在人工智能推理引擎、逻辑编程语言和法律推理系统中发挥核心作用，让抽象的形式工具与真实世界的问题求解紧密相连。\n\n建议自学者先完成形式逻辑的基本训练，再并行探索非形式逻辑与数理逻辑，最后进入应用章节。大量的习题练习和实际论证分析是学好逻辑的关键。\n","chapters":[{"seq":1,"slug":"formal-logic","title":"形式逻辑","docCount":3,"url":"/education/university/philosophy/logic/formal-logic","docs":[{"seq":1,"slug":"propositional-logic","title":"命题逻辑","url":"/education/university/philosophy/logic/formal-logic/propositional-logic"},{"seq":2,"slug":"predicate-logic","title":"谓词逻辑","url":"/education/university/philosophy/logic/formal-logic/predicate-logic"},{"seq":3,"slug":"modal-logic","title":"模态逻辑","url":"/education/university/philosophy/logic/formal-logic/modal-logic"}]},{"seq":2,"slug":"informal-logic","title":"非形式逻辑","docCount":3,"url":"/education/university/philosophy/logic/informal-logic","docs":[{"seq":1,"slug":"argumentation-theory","title":"论证理论","url":"/education/university/philosophy/logic/informal-logic/argumentation-theory"},{"seq":2,"slug":"logical-fallacies","title":"逻辑谬误","url":"/education/university/philosophy/logic/informal-logic/logical-fallacies"},{"seq":3,"slug":"critical-thinking","title":"批判性思维","url":"/education/university/philosophy/logic/informal-logic/critical-thinking"}]},{"seq":3,"slug":"mathematical-logic","title":"数理逻辑","docCount":3,"url":"/education/university/philosophy/logic/mathematical-logic","docs":[{"seq":1,"slug":"set-theory-foundations","title":"集合论基础","url":"/education/university/philosophy/logic/mathematical-logic/set-theory-foundations"},{"seq":2,"slug":"model-theory","title":"模型论","url":"/education/university/philosophy/logic/mathematical-logic/model-theory"},{"seq":3,"slug":"computability-theory","title":"可计算性理论","url":"/education/university/philosophy/logic/mathematical-logic/computability-theory"}]},{"seq":4,"slug":"applied-logic","title":"应用逻辑","docCount":3,"url":"/education/university/philosophy/logic/applied-logic","docs":[{"seq":1,"slug":"logic-in-ai","title":"逻辑与人工智能","url":"/education/university/philosophy/logic/applied-logic/logic-in-ai"},{"seq":2,"slug":"logic-programming","title":"逻辑编程","url":"/education/university/philosophy/logic/applied-logic/logic-programming"},{"seq":3,"slug":"legal-reasoning","title":"法律推理","url":"/education/university/philosophy/logic/applied-logic/legal-reasoning"}]}]}